Thermal rocket propulsion analysis and design practical. The work centres about preparing, executing, analysing and reporting a
rocket motor functional test. The aim of this test is to determine how well the motor performs and determine motor quality as
well as the quality of its main components (chamber and nozzle). For a given motor* students are asked to:
1. predict motor performances from theoretical analysis/simulations performed;
2. devise a test plan including at least a description of the item to be tested, test objective(s), test approach with short description
of planned test(s), test equipment and instrumentation, required calibrations, pass/fail criteria, test risks/issues, test deliverables);
3. prepare the test (assemble motor and install it on the thrust bench) and perform test readiness review;
4. test the motor;
5. discuss the test data obtained and draw inferences;
6. compare test data with simulation results and draw inferences;
7. report work done.
* Last year we conducted a test on either a small solid rocket motor or a water rocket.

