At the end of the course, the students will be able to:
- Compute (conditional) probabilities;
- Perform computations with discrete and continuous random variables and apply the law of large numbers and the central limit
theorem;
- Identify and use numerical values that summarize the information contained in random variables;
- Relate random variables to statistical experiments and select statistical models suitable for describing real-life situations;
- Analyze data by means of graphical and numerical summaries;
- Define and evaluate statistical procedures for conducting statistical inference (estimation and hypothesis testing).

Knowledge
