learning_objectives:
Students will be able to
(cid:9)explain the concept of multimedia;
(cid:9)explain the principles underlying basic multimedia search engines;
(cid:9)explain the functioning of basic multimedia recommender systems;
(cid:9)describe and implement common representations of multimedia content;
(cid:9)describe and implement common ranking mechanisms for multimedia search;
(cid:9)describe and implement common recommender system techniques;
(cid:9)describe and implement common social media analytics techniques for multimedia search and recommendation;
(cid:9)interpret current academic literature in the field of multimedia search and recommendation;
(cid:9)identify strengths and weaknesses of state-of-the-art multimedia search and recommendation functionalities;
(cid:9)identify challenges belonging to the development of multimedia search and recommendation functionalities;
(cid:9)identify evaluation criteria for multimedia search engines and recommender systems;
(cid:9)explain the difference between topical relevance and utility in multimedia search and recommendation;
(cid:9)describe and implement cross-disciplinary approaches to multimedia search and recommendation;
(cid:9)describe and implement practical solutions to deal with real-world multimedia search and/or recommendation;
