After successful completion of the course, you:
1. Know, understand and can apply (3) the functionality, construction and application of active implantable biomedical
microsystems (AIBMs) and their sub-systems and parts;
2. Know, understand and can apply (3) the fundamental principles and approaches for designing an implantable system;
3. Know, understand, can apply, analyse and can reason about (evaluate; 5) the design requirements, application-specific
implementation challenges, and appropriate design choices of existing AIBMs, incl. cardiac pacemakers, cochlear implants and
spinal cord stimulators;
4. Know and understand (2) the most important implantability, biocompatibility, reliability, safety and security issues of
AIBMs;
5. Know and understand (2) the most important regulatory and clinical constraints of AIBMs
6. Can reason (5) about future developments of AIBMs, a.o. electroceuticals and bioelectronic medicine;
NB. The numbers correspond with Bloom's taxonomy.

