After this course students have to be able
* to recognize and explain different mechanisms of electromagnetic waves (EMW) propagation/scattering and relations between
them;
* to assess different mechanisms of EMW propagation/scattering in relation to characteristics of EMW and media;
* to estimate quantitatively the influence of the propagation and scattering mechanisms on trade-offs that have to be made when
designing a wireless communication or sensing system.
* to analyze real-world scenarios and identify the involved propagation and scattering mechanisms and their relevant aspects;

