description:
The following subjects are discussed:
- winding function and inductances;
- time and spatial harmonics;
- skin effect in electrical machines;
- phasor, space vector and transformation in electrical machines;
- the salient pole synchronous machine;
- modeling and simulation of the dynamic performance of DC and AC machines.

learning_objectives:
After following this course the students should be able to
- describe and calculate the steady-state performance of AC machines;
- calculate spatial harmonics and inductances of given winding distributions;
- derive the dynamic models of DC and AC machines using space vectors;
- model and simulate the dynamic performance of DC and AC machines;
- evaluate the limitations of the dynamic models.

