The student is able to select and make an hydraulic and heat technical design of heat transfer equipment.
More specifically, the student:
1.(cid:9)Can quantify heat transfer by conduction, convection & radiation in process equipment;
2.(cid:9)Can estimate the heat transfer by condensation and boiling;
3.(cid:9)Can calculate overall heat transfer coefficients;
4.(cid:9)Can select heat transfer equipment for given application;
5.(cid:9)Can apply effectiveness and Number of Transfer Units method in heat exchanger design;
6.(cid:9)Can design & analyse shell-and-tube heat exchangers (with / without phase change);
7.(cid:9)Can design & analyse plate heat exchangers (with / without phase change)
8.(cid:9)Can design & analyse finned-tube heat exchangers (with / without phase change);
9.(cid:9)Can design & analyse furnaces;
10.(cid:9)Can apply pinch technology / heat integration / exergy analysis for heat exchanger network.
Furthermore, the student is able to make a design of thermal separation processes, including the dimensioning of the equipment.
More specifically, the student:
11.(cid:9)Can describe the characteristics and principles of the most relevant thermal separation processes,
12.(cid:9)Can describe and formulate thermodynamics equations and models for the selection and design of thermal separation
processes,
13.(cid:9)Can quantify the mass transfer rate over an interface by diffusion end convection,
14.(cid:9)Knows the role of mass transfer in the dimensioning of equipment for separation processes
15.(cid:9)Can determine the separation efficiency for single and multi-stage separations and can quantify the influence of the process
conditions and the contacting modes on the separation.
16.(cid:9)Can describe principles and design methods for processes and equipment used in equilibrium stage separation processes, such
as distillation, absorption, stripping (desorption), extraction, crystallization and membrane separations
17.(cid:9)Can use computer based process simulation tools to analyse and design separation equipment
18.(cid:9)Can design and analyse thermal separation process including dimensioning of the equipment.

After successful completion of this course, the student is able to independently:
1.(cid:9)Apply electrochemical nomenclature to describe the electrochemical cell and electrochemical measurements;
2.(cid:9)Explain the concept of the electrochemical double layer and mass transport in the electrolyte;
3.(cid:9)Apply basic principles of electrochemical thermodynamics, such as the Nernst equation, overpotentials and (standard)
equilibrium potentials;
4.(cid:9)Apply basic principles of electrochemical kinetics, such as the Tafel equation and the Buttler-Volmer model;
5.(cid:9)Explain the principles that determine the electrocatalytic performance of materials;
6.(cid:9)Interpret scientific literature reports on electrochemical energy storage and conversion systems and devices.

