learning_objectives:
At the end of the course, students are expected to have gained knowledge on principles of high-tech marketing and will be able
to recognize, analyze, reflect upon, and creatively respond to, high-tech marketing problems and challenges with regard to:
- Marketing strategies and plans to deal with uncertainty in high-tech environments;
- Customer segmentation, targeting, and positioning for business-to-business (B2B) and business-to-consumer (B2C) markets;
- Product and service bundles development, (offline and online) word-of-mouth, advertising and promotion, incl. modern online
tools;
- Some marketing research techniques (various methodologies) aimed at analyzing customer preferences for regular as well as
persuasive (Web 2.0/3.0) marketing strategic communications and technologies (recommender systems).

