Analyze relevant aspects of logistics and transportation system: inventory, routing, location, data;
Formulate (and solve) a selection of relevant logistics problems;
Select and apply an appropriate methodology for a given logistics problem;
Find possibilities to improve/adapt a logistics system through data and analytical models;
Model operational aspects through mathematical linear programming models;
Understand the integrative role of logistics function in and between organizations;

After this course students are able to:
(cid:9)Reproduce and interpret knowledge about frugal innovation from a technology perspective;
(cid:9)Apply this perspective critically to case studies from different parts of the world;
(cid:9)Analyse and interpret the potential of frugal innovation in the pursuit of the UN Sustainable Development Goals from a
technology perspective;
(cid:9)Learn from other disciplines, in particular innovation theories and management as well as specific technology disciplines, and
relate this knowledge to and integrate into their own disciplinary background, and
(cid:9)Make a constructive contribution to the debate on frugal innovation and sustainable global development.

After successfully completing the course, the participants will be able to:
1) Understand the principles of the selected research approaches and methods;
2) Reflect on the strengths and limitations of the research methods and analysis techniques;
3) Create a research project plan with substantial research methods, finance strategy and risk and safety plan for the upcoming
intercultural field research.
4) Set up at least 5 expert consultation meetings to prepare and reflect on the upcoming field project;
5) Design and present a detailed project research plan for the upcoming intercultural internship.

(1) learn how to be a good steward of your business and critically assess financial viability of a business model;
(2) know where you can obtain funds for your business, the trade-offs with each funding source, and how it fits your business
model;
(3) become well-versed in fundraising strategy;
(4) master or review fundamental concepts in finance.

