By the end of the Experience Entrepreneurship programme, students should be able to:
- Understand the basic principles of entrepreneurship;
- Define a case study topic.
- Analyze and summarize the problem, defined at the beginning of the case study, and evaluate the possible solutions both
theoretically as well as practically by means of research questions;
- Understand what it takes to be an (sustainable) entrepreneur;
- Develop insights into what their own motivations, ambitions and objectives are as (potential) entrepreneurs;

