learning_objectives:
At the end of the course, the students will know:
- the basics of Ito calculus;
- the fundamentals of asset pricing;
- how to change measure and the impact of such an operation in pricing and financial mathematics;
- the importance of risk-neutrality;
- how to price the most important derivatives;
- how to deal with some of the most important issues in risk management (VaR, error estimation, loss estimation);
- how basic exchange and interest rates work and how they can be efficiently modeled.

By the end of this course, students will be able to
- Recognize convex sets and their applications;
- Apply the theory of convexity to concrete examples;
- State the main results/theorems concerning polyhedra;
- Model problems as linear programming problems;
- Recognize total unimodularity and use it to prove integrality of polyhedra;
- Construct the dual of a linear program.

