Upon successful completion of this course, the student
1. knows and understands the objective of statistical learning and the curse of dimensionality in the context of statistical learning;
2. can apply and analyse relevant models for statistical learning, including linear regression, logistic regression, sparse regression
models, support vector machines and neural networks;
3. can apply and analyse ways for avoiding overfitting in the context of statistical learning;
4. can apply and analyse methods for extending, combining and selecting models, such as kernel methods and cross validation;
5. can apply and analyse computational methods and algorithms used in statistical learning, such as stochastic gradient descent.

